"Experimental: Vulkan runs through MoltenVK on top of Metal. Some games may draw wrongly or stop, and if Vulkan fails the next launch switches back to Metal." = "Experimental: Vulkan runs through MoltenVK on top of Metal. Some games may draw wrongly or stop, and if Vulkan fails the next launch switches back to Metal.";
"Export all settings" = "Export all settings";
"Export all settings writes one .json file to Files: every setting, and the settings you've set for individual games. It never includes your library, favourites, Wii U keys, accounts, theme or premium unlock.\n\nImport settings reads such a file, checks it, and asks before it replaces anything. Importing replaces all your settings and every game's own options with what the file holds, and anything the file doesn't mention goes back to its default. Some changes apply the next time you start a game." = "Export all settings writes one .json file to Files: every setting, and the settings you've set for individual games. It never includes your library, favourites, Wii U keys, accounts, theme or premium unlock.\n\nImport settings reads such a file, checks it, and asks before it replaces anything. Importing replaces all your settings and every game's own options with what the file holds, and anything the file doesn't mention goes back to its default. Some changes apply the next time you start a game.";
"Export cancelled." = "Export cancelled.";
"Export colours (.muffinclr)" = "Export colours (.muffinclr)";
"Export everything" = "Export everything";
"Export everything writes one file to Files, in MuffinEMU > Migration. It holds your saves, installed updates and DLC, accounts, keys.txt, otp.bin and seeprom.bin, compiled shader caches, graphic packs, save states, settings, favourites and appearance.\n\nGames (the Roms folder, and base games installed into the Wii U storage) are left out unless you turn on Include games. Without them the export is much smaller, and you can copy your games into the new app in Files. Screen recordings, save backups, logs and other caches are never included. The premium unlock isn't carried over; enter it again in the new app.\n\nThe export runs only while MuffinEMU is open on screen, and keeps the screen awake. You can stop it at any time. Before it starts, MuffinEMU checks that there's enough free space, and the file is kept out of device backups.\n\nWhen it's done, share the file to the new MuffinEMU's Files folder or to another device, install the new MuffinEMU, and choose Import from the old MuffinEMU there. Delete the export afterwards to get the space back." = "Export everything writes one file to Files, in MuffinEMU > Migration. It holds your saves, installed updates and DLC, accounts, keys.txt, otp.bin and seeprom.bin, compiled shader caches, graphic packs, save states, settings, favourites and appearance.\n\nGames (the Roms folder, and base games installed into the Wii U storage) are left out unless you turn on Include games. Without them the export is much smaller, and you can copy your games into the new app in Files. Screen recordings, save backups, logs and other caches are never included. The premium unlock isn't carried over; enter it again in the new app.\n\nThe export runs only while MuffinEMU is open on screen, and keeps the screen awake. You can stop it at any time. Before it starts, MuffinEMU checks that there's enough free space, and the file is kept out of device backups.\n\nWhen it's done, share the file to the new MuffinEMU's Files folder or to another device, install the new MuffinEMU, and choose Import from the old MuffinEMU there. Delete the export afterwards to get the space back.";
