"Performance profile" = "Performance profile";
"Performance profile picks one trade-off. Balanced is the default.\n\nAccuracy is slower but can fix a game that glitches, desyncs or crashes. It runs on one CPU core and builds every shader before it is needed, whatever Compile shaders in the background is set to.\n\nSpeed is the opposite trade: everything runs as fast as MuffinEMU can make it, and some quality goes. The picture is drawn at Balanced at most with linear scaling, so it's softer. Shaders skip the Wii U's exact multiply rule, which is faster but can make lighting or shadows look wrong in some games. Shaders always compile in the background, so things can pop in for a moment instead of the game pausing. Crash reports carry less detail.\n\nBattery saver runs on one CPU core whatever CPU cores is set to, for less heat and battery use, at some cost in frame rate.\n\nA game can have its own profile in its Game settings.\n\nPause the TV screen and Pause the GamePad screen stop drawing whichever Wii U screen is out of sight while Screen Layout is Single Screen. The game keeps running and the screen picks up again the moment you swap to it. The same two switches are under Display.\n\nCool down automatically acts when iOS reports the device is overheating, and Device heat shows that same state. In Advanced mode, Cool down starts at picks the point: Serious (the default) acts as soon as iOS starts throttling, Critical waits until iOS is throttling hard.\n\nThe profile applies the next time you start a game." = "Performance profile picks one trade-off. Balanced is the default.\n\nAccuracy is slower but can fix a game that glitches, desyncs or crashes. It runs on one CPU core and builds every shader before it is needed, whatever Compile shaders in the background is set to.\n\nSpeed is the opposite trade: everything runs as fast as MuffinEMU can make it, and some quality goes. The picture is drawn at Balanced at most with linear scaling, so it's softer. Shaders skip the Wii U's exact multiply rule, which is faster but can make lighting or shadows look wrong in some games. Shaders always compile in the background, so things can pop in for a moment instead of the game pausing. Crash reports carry less detail.\n\nBattery saver runs on one CPU core whatever CPU cores is set to, for less heat and battery use, at some cost in frame rate.\n\nA game can have its own profile in its Game settings.\n\nPause the TV screen and Pause the GamePad screen stop drawing whichever Wii U screen is out of sight while Screen Layout is Single Screen. The game keeps running and the screen picks up again the moment you swap to it. The same two switches are under Display.\n\nCool down automatically acts when iOS reports the device is overheating, and Device heat shows that same state. In Advanced mode, Cool down starts at picks the point: Serious (the default) acts as soon as iOS starts throttling, Critical waits until iOS is throttling hard.\n\nThe profile applies the next time you start a game.";
"Persistent ID" = "Persistent ID";
"Pick" = "Pick";
"Pick a pack folder, a folder that holds several packs, or a zip of either. MuffinEMU checks that it really contains a pack (a rules.txt) before adding it.\n\nImported packs are kept apart from the community download, so updating the community packs never removes them. Importing the same folder name again replaces the earlier copy. To remove an imported pack, open it and choose Remove.\n\nYou can also drop pack folders into graphicPacks inside MuffinEMU's Documents folder in Files." = "Pick a pack folder, a folder that holds several packs, or a zip of either. MuffinEMU checks that it really contains a pack (a rules.txt) before adding it.\n\nImported packs are kept apart from the community download, so updating the community packs never removes them. Importing the same folder name again replaces the earlier copy. To remove an imported pack, open it and choose Remove.\n\nYou can also drop pack folders into graphicPacks inside MuffinEMU's Documents folder in Files.";
"Pick an amiibo dump (.bin or .nfc). MuffinEMU keeps a copy in Documents/amiibo so you can scan it again with one tap. The game has to be asking for an amiibo when you scan." = "Pick an amiibo dump (.bin or .nfc). MuffinEMU keeps a copy in Documents/amiibo so you can scan it again with one tap. The game has to be asking for an amiibo when you scan.";
"Pick an image from Files, iCloud Drive, or another app." = "Pick an image from Files, iCloud Drive, or another app.";
"Pick the .muffinmove file you exported from the old MuffinEMU. It can be on this device or in iCloud Drive. This also works to restore your data after reinstalling MuffinEMU.\n\nMuffinEMU checks the file first and shows what it would change. Files that aren't here yet are added, and files that are older than the export's are updated. If a file here is newer than the export's copy, you choose whether to keep it or replace it; saves that are replaced are moved to save-backups first, not deleted. Every file is checked as it is copied, so a damaged export can't leave a half-written file behind, and an interrupted import can simply be run again.\n\nIt works only while MuffinEMU is open on screen. When it finishes, close MuffinEMU and open it again." = "Pick the .muffinmove file you exported from the old MuffinEMU. It can be on this device or in iCloud Drive. This also works to restore your data after reinstalling MuffinEMU.\n\nMuffinEMU checks the file first and shows what it would change. Files that aren't here yet are added, and files that are older than the export's are updated. If a file here is newer than the export's copy, you choose whether to keep it or replace it; saves that are replaced are moved to save-backups first, not deleted. Every file is checked as it is copied, so a damaged export can't leave a half-written file behind, and an interrupted import can simply be run again.\n\nIt works only while MuffinEMU is open on screen. When it finishes, close MuffinEMU and open it again.";
